  <p>Each profile below combines facts about a household in PA-3 with the system components that affect that household. The toggles above let you read the page through four analytical lenses:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Neutral analytical</strong> (both off, default) — the mechanical facts without editorial framing. Useful when you want the data without the interpretation.</li>
    <li><strong>Synthesis</strong> (both on) — the full picture; both how the system delivers and where it fails.</li>
    <li><strong>Design view</strong> — what the system delivers, framed around the mechanism. Useful for understanding what's available, who can claim it, how to engage with the system as it currently operates.</li>
    <li><strong>Gap view</strong> — where the system fails, framed around the failure pathway. Useful for understanding what's not working, who falls through, what reform proposals address it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>All four are valid lenses on the same underlying data. The page is not reduced or filtered in any mode; you are reading the same analytical work with different emphasis.</p>
</details>

